# Debian revisions, read by scripts/build-deb.sh: one line per entry,
#   <package> <upstream version> <revision>
# package: pwsh or pwsh-preview; upstream version: Microsoft's tag without
# the v (7.7.0, 7.8.0-preview.1); revision: a positive integer, no leading 0.
# A release with no line here is revision 1. Bump the revision to re-release
# the same PowerShell build under a new version and release tag (a packaging
# fix, or a tag name GitHub has retired). Keep a line while its version is
# built: removing it takes the package back to revision 1, a downgrade.
# Docs: docs/markDown/engineering/architecture/packaging.md#revisions

# The release and tag pwsh-7.7.0-1 were deleted; GitHub never reuses the tag
# name of a deleted immutable release.
pwsh 7.7.0 2
